  "description": "Our entry model to our MISSION gravel racing family. Featuring the same CF4 carbon frame as the top models but is equipped with a more wallet-friendly yet gravel-proven specification package.\n\nFast, capable and composed. Our entry-level carbon MISSION 4000 is designed for the high-speed, high-stakes world of gravel racing and is based on our latest CF4 carbon fibre gravel race frame. Add high-volume, fast-rolling, off-road-tough gravel tyres, Shimano's proven GRX groupset, Shimano wheels, and a flared handlebar to maximise control on rough tracks, and you have the perfect mix of low weight, sharp but stable handling, and comfort — ideal for fast-paced gravel rides or rough road routes.\n\nOur new MISSION truly embodies its ‘fast on any surface’ intentions. It is a gravel race bike that combines key geometry and frame elements from the SCULTURA ENDURANCE and the SILEX, sprinkles them with a heavy dose of road racing DNA to deliver a fast and responsive ride on pretty much any surface.\n\nWhether you're tackling fast-paced gravel races to tarmac-based chain gang outings, the MISSION delivers. With up to 40 mm tyre clearance, there is scope for wider gravel racing tyres or large volume road tyres, and its low weight of around 7.8 kg of the 10K model makes it fly up the hills, keeps it super responsive and catapults it out of corners. The MISSION’s built-in storage compartment improves the accessibility and organisation of crucial mid-race nutrition and spares, further enhancing the efficiency when every second counts.\n\nFinally, the ability to seamlessly fit 1x or 2x drivetrains gives riders more flexibility to find their preferred setup for whatever riding or racing style they want to focus on. Welcome to your MISSION - Fast on any surface.\n\n\"Fast, versatile, fun and the perfect all-road and gravel race bike\", so the summarised statements of a long list of international cycling titles like Bikerumor, Gran Fondo, Bikeboard, Road.cc and RadFahren (just to name a few) when they put our MISSION through its paces.",
